  "verbalization": "Notoamide B is implicated in the regulation of CX-1 through multiple pathways, with the target entity Malme-3M acting as a common intermediary in all three evidence chains. The drug is shown to interact with Malme-3M, which is a target of three different compounds—Linustatin, Methyl 4-Formylbenzoate, and Ingenol-20-decanoate—all of which ultimately target CX-1. This suggests a potential mechanism where Notoamide B modulates Malme-3M, which in turn influences CX-1 through a shared biological process. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically supported relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction between Notoamide B and Malme-3M remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting Malme-3M and CX-1 implies that the pathway may involve a broader network of molecular interactions, potentially involving signaling pathways or cellular processes that are yet to be fully characterized.",
